    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d778">

                <pb facs="0722" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg710"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/6–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-27T23:00:00-04:00">June 27, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5065. Please inform the Foreign Office that we should appreciate being informed
                    as soon as possible whether the appropriate British <pb facs="0723" n="711"
                        xml:id="pg711"/> authorities concur in the joint goods subsidy program for
                    Saudi Arabia worked out in Cairo by Mr. Landis and British representatives
                    there, who are understood to have referred their suggested program to London for
                        approval.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d778-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d778-f1" n="16" xml:id="d778-f1-content">
                <p>In his telegram 5271, July 4, 6 p.m., the Ambassador in the United Kingdom
                    reported that he had been informed by the British Foreign Office that “the
                    British Embassy in Washington has been instructed to inform the Department of
                    the British Government’s reaction to the joint goods subsidy program for Saudi
                    Arabia.” (890F.24/7–444)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
